The takeoff was unremarkable. The plane reached a cruising altitude of 35,000 feet. The passengers read and watched movies and slept. As they flew over the Atlantic Ocean passing the equator, there was a lot of thunderstorm activity quite typical, nothing really unusual about that. That's William Longavicia. He wrote an article for Vanity Fair about this flight and has written extensively about aviation. He also used to be a pilot. So I spent many, many thousands of hours in cockpits.
起飞过程很平稳。飞机爬升到了 35,000 英尺的巡航高度。乘客们看书、看电影、睡觉。当他们飞越跨过赤道的大西洋上空时，有许多雷暴活动，这很典型，并没有什么真正不寻常的地方。这是威廉·隆加维西亚（William Longavicia）。他为《名利场》（Vanity Fair）杂志写过一篇关于这次航班的文章，并且在航空领域进行过大量写作。他以前也是一名飞行员。所以我花了好几千个小时在驾驶舱里。

